  "why": "The statement is for every smooth projective variety in all genera, so every restricted proof is a case. Before the snapshot: genus 0 (Liu-Tian), semisimple targets (Dubrovin-Zhang, Givental, Teleman), curves (Okounkov-Pandharipande), Grassmannians and Calabi-Yau threefolds are cases. Conditional reductions (Coates-Givental-Tseng, Liu 2001, Tseng 2026, OpenAI projectivization) prove nothing outright, so they are none. Sheaf, quiver, stable-pair, Hodge-integral, orbifold-curve and one-derivative results are variants. After the snapshot, Guo-Zhang-Zhou (genus one, Fano complete intersections, ambient classes) is a human case. The OpenAI complete-intersection manuscript is a case: it covers complete intersections in P^N only, not all varieties. It is unreviewed and doubtful but not not_credible: the manuscript was read, it is serious and detailed, and it has been public for only a week. Its AI role is generated because the authors' README says the model produced the manuscripts. Hashemi et al. is none: the network modelled known point-case constraints and proved nothing.",
